RARDecode is a Swift port of the decompression code in the UnRAR source by
Alexander L. Roshal / RARLAB (https://www.rarlab.com). The unRAR license requires the following paragraph to be reproduced:

   UnRAR source code may be used in any software to handle
   RAR archives without limitations free of charge, but cannot be
   used to develop RAR (WinRAR) compatible archiver and to
   re-create RAR compression algorithm, which is proprietary.
   Distribution of modified UnRAR source code in separate form
   or as a part of other software is permitted, provided that
   full text of this paragraph, starting from "UnRAR source code"
   words, is included in license, or in documentation if license
   is not available, and in source code comments of resulting package.

The PPMd model and its memory allocator in RARDecode (PPMdModel.swift,
PPMdHeap.swift) follow UnRAR's model.cpp and suballoc.cpp, which are based on
PPMd variant H by Dmitry Shkarin (public domain); the range decoder follows
UnRAR's coder.cpp, after the carryless range coder by Dmitry Subbotin.

The tests contain a small bit writer (RAR5Stream in Unpack50Tests.swift) that
encodes the symbols a test gives it with fixed, flat Huffman tables, to build
rare or malformed RAR5 streams. It searches for no matches and is not a RAR
compressor; it is original code and not derived from UnRAR.

SwiftRAR is a reader only. It does not and must never create or compress RAR
archives.

The UnRAR source itself is not part of this repository.
Tools/oracle/build-unrar.sh downloads it (UnRAR 7.3.1) solely to build the
official unrar binary as a test oracle; it is never linked into the package.
